A new message appears on my phone screen.
It says that my identity must be verified.
"A one-time code will be sent via text message," the system writes.
I read the instructions at the bottom of the screen.
"Please wait."
"Do not close the page."
I look at my phone and wait.
The screen remains blank, and nothing happens.
Ten seconds pass.
Twenty seconds pass.
I sigh quietly to myself.
I am starting to get a little annoyed.
These automated codes usually arrive immediately.
Normally it only takes a second.
But my inbox is still empty.
I check the clock on the phone.
Maybe the system is just slow this evening?
I decide to wait one more minute.
If the code is not sent soon, I will have to try again.
